1. `vm.c:1360` - when loading a BIGINT pool literal (from compiled bytecode)
2. `string.c:2385` - when parsing a string to integer with overflow

The fuzzer uses `mrb_load_string` which compiles Ruby source code. So the path through `string.c:2385` is the most accessible - we need a string that, when converted to an integer, overflows and triggers the bigint path.

